WEBVTT

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.360
I never knew Yumoto's brother made soba.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.930
So he can do more than just chop wood.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.080
Yeah!

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.330
Today we'll eat Gora's 
hand-made New Year's soba,

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:21.740
then listen to the New Year's bell

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.660
and make our first shrine visit 
of the new year together!

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.380
Then we'll watch the first sunrise

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.490
and eat our New Year's feast together...

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.920
I'm looking forward to it so much!

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.820
What are you talking about?

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.640
Once I'm out of this bath, I'm 
eating soba and heading home.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:37.340
Same here.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.090
Huh? Senpais, you're just going home?

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.620
I'm going, too.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:45.440
For the New Year, I always visit a shrine 
to Benzaiten to pray for my stocks to go up.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.040
I'm going to the daruma fair with some girls.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.450
The daruma fair?

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.070
We were supposed to go snowboarding,

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.150
but it's so cold it got to be 
more trouble than it was worth.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:59.280
Speaking of which, didn't we have plans 
to go skiing during winter break?

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.530
Yes.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:03.780
Though sadly we had to cancel because Yumoto

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.840
couldn't save up enough allowance.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.050
I tried really hard,

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.670
but I just couldn't seem to save it up!

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.460
What is your allowance, anyway?

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.520
500 yen per month!

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.230
Are you a child?!

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:51.810
Love is Like the Snow

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.920
Everyone's going home after the soba...

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.870
it's gonna be a lonely New Year...

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.230
What's the big deal?

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.910
Go on your first shrine visit with Gora.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.300
That's right.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.880
Make it a brother thing.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:08.910
Yeah!

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:12.330
Wouldn't that be a nice way 
to kick off the year, Yumoto?

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.450
Just me and Gora?

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.880
Yeah, good idea!

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:18.920
Okay!

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.450
Then after we eat the soba,

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.840
me and my bro will go for 
our first shrine visit...

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.900
and watch the first sunrise 
of the New Year together!

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:25.550
What?

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.340
Yumoto doesn't just get to eat 
Gora-san's New Year's soba...

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:32.180
...he gets to spend the first shrine visit 
and first sunrise of the New Year alone with him?

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.860
Such an active and marvelous New Year.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.850
We will...

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.290
...never let it happen!

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:44.060
He doesn't get the day off 
off, even on New Year?

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.330
The Andromeda calendar isn't like Japan's.

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.540
Let's watch CIDE and wait, Haru.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:56.790
<b>Due to a cosmic storm, your scheduled programming will not be seen today</b>

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:56.210
Due to a cosmic storm, your scheduled 
programming will not be seen today.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.760
Andromeda Ramen Battle!!

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.760
<b>Andromeda Ramen Battle!!</b>

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.320
You're kidding me!

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.470
How can the broadcast be canceled?

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:08.930
Hey, you two.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:11.840
Could you help me get ready 
for the mochi-pounding?

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:13.390
It's really hard doing it alone!

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:14.640
Dadacha.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:15.850
We'll do the mochi-pounding later.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:21.580
First, we're going to ruin 
their New Year's soba!

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.370
Then we're going to unveil the special New 
Year's gift we've been holding in reserve!

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.040
<b>Tomorrow's
 Weather</b>

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.040
<i>It'll be cold, but clear 
skies all over Japan.</i>

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:34.210
Hey, the Pink Song Battle is about to start!

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.680
What are you talking about?

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.440
On New Year's Eve,

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.410
you have to watch "Classic Japanese 
Melodies to End the Year."

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:42.500
Huh?

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.390
Don't you watch the "Don't Get Mad" series?

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.320
It's ending this year, you know!

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.560
The World Ham Walk

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.560
No, on New Year's Eve you're 
supposed to put in a DVD!

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.500
No, since the markets are closed for the day,

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.320
my New Year's tradition is getting 
fired up watching martial arts!

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:09.740
Earth New Year's Eve is filled with 
so many different kinds of love!

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.690
<b>Gokaku Cram School</b>

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.920
<b>Jinzou Makoto</b>

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.160
This spring, we'll be in art school!

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.350
We just have to buckle down 
for New Year's, that's all.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.300
We've gotta get into college 
on our first try, right?

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.030
Haru.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:34.470
I see a good one.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.560
Yeah.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.760
Hey, Senpai.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.730
Senpai?

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:48.320
Yes, we're students at Binan 
High School, just like you.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.500
Oh... r-really?

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:55.580
Although we have very little in 
common with a 23-year-old senpai

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:59.490
who's spent five years failing 
to get accepted into college.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.540
H-How did you know that?

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.670
Senpai, really.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:08.060
You think "I'm actually a genius 
who will change the world"

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.680
or something, don't you?

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:15.770
Yet they won't acknowledge your 
genius, so you just continue failing.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.740
Even your parents are fed up with you.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:22.580
You borrow money to go to cram schools with 
no hope of ever paying back your debts.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:28.450
And yet you think it's all the fault of the 
people refusing to accept you into college.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.370
Yeah, that's right!

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:34.280
It's not my fault I've been 
rejected for five years!

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:38.140
The university people just don't 
appreciate my shining art talent!

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:42.000
If I keep failing, my debts 
will just keep snowballing...

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:46.130
I'm never going to escape this winter.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.740
So, why not show them that shining talent?

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:52.080
You want to draw

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:55.680
an incredible picture that will 
change the whole world, don't you?

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:04.790
We gotta watch Classic Japanese 
Melodies for New Year's, huh?

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:07.360
We decided with rock paper 
scissors. What can you do?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.820
His vibrato is <i>the best</i>.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.130
After we eat, I'm going home.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:15.870
Yumoto, when's the soba coming?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.950
Bro Gora just put it in the 
water, so it'll be done soon!

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.180
Is this kotatsu a little cold?

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:22.290
I'm gonna get a chill from the bath.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.750
Then let's set it to maximum!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.800
The heater doesn't seem to 
be working well, either.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:30.730
Here's what I do at times like this!

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:32.520
Toasty!

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.400
Hey, that's ours!

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.140
Bro Gora's gonna be so mad!

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.850
<b>Do Not Remove
Kurotama Bath</b>

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.850
It says "Do not remove"!

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.110
Then how about this?

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.810
Toasty!

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.020
Yumoto, it's done.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.020
Yeah!

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.090
I'll bring the stew by later.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:51.490
Eat them before they get soggy, everyone.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.740
Let's eat!

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.130
Here's your first mission...

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:57.700
Snowman Monster!

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.610
What happened?

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.010
It seems to be a power outage.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.470
Hey, the power went out 
before we even did anything.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.680
Yumoto, where's the flashlight?

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.250
I'm looking for it!

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:24.050
That's my leg!

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:25.890
That's my head!

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:26.990
Really.

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:30.620
This is why you should have a disaster 
readiness kit, just in case.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.550
Hey, it's back on!

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.860
Great!

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:39.770
Not great.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.290
The song is over.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:43.500
Too bad, huh, En-chan?

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:47.810
Anyway, let's eat our soba before the 
power goes out again, then get going.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:51.090
They're soggy...

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:55.090
They used that power outage to 
take the wind out of our sails!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.760
Even more unforgivable!

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:59.100
Go, Snowman Monster!

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.510
The land is my canvas!

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:08.230
I'll paint it in my image!

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.800
My canvas!

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.960
<i>Thank you very much!</i>

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:23.690
<i>On New Year's, eat mochi, mochi, mochi!</i>

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.370
Okay,

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:23.690
I'd better get going.

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:25.080
Thanks for the meal, Yumoto.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.040
I think I'll head home, too.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:27.650
Huh?

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.500
You're really leaving?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.250
It's about time for me, too.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:32.210
And me.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.020
Well, see you!

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:36.700
Have a happy New Year!

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.010
Huh?

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:40.510
It won't open!

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:43.300
Yumoto.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.930
Did you lock the door so we couldn't leave?

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:47.600
Of course not!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.880
What's with all this snow?

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.310
It wasn't coming down at all before...

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:59.220
And the weather forecast said it would 
be clear skies all over the country...

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:03.640
They won't be able to get out.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:06.750
Now we'll send them the present 
we've been holding onto.

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:09.660
Snowman Monster, third mission!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.740
Looks like we'll be having 
New Year's at Yumoto's house.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:18.260
Yeah, there's just too much snow.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.660
Ten seconds to the new year!

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:25.700
Five!

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:26.680
Four!

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:27.630
Three!

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:28.670
Two!

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:29.690
One!

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.180
Happy New Year!

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:37.070
Happy Snow Year!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.070
A snowman!

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:43.290
I'm Snowman Monster!

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:45.790
To celebrate the new year, 
I'll paint you in my image!

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:48.540
Close the freaking window, 
it's cold out there!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:49.680
Yeah, c'mon.

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:50.460
It's cold.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:52.680
Hey!

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:54.250
A monster just showed up!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:54.720
Come on!

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.090
Stand up and fight!

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.830
Can't you give us New Year's off?

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:00.180
There's no way we can fight 
in this cold. No way.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:01.510
I can't leave the kotatsu.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:02.660
I <i>will</i> not.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.010
Wom-san's all curled up 
under the kotatsu, too!

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.090
Working the New Year's 
holiday demands a pay bump.

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:09.980
And it's currently midnight,

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.980
so we'd need a late night bonus, too...

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:13.940
Oh no!

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.650
Don't go to any trouble.

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:16.620
Then it's settled.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.430
We're taking the holiday off.

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:19.920
It's decided.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:22.950
Cheers!

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:27.660
I bet they've all been 
turned into snowmen by now.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.180
Take that, Yumoto!

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.620
Take that, Defense Club!

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:35.590
Go on, eat your New Year's stew!

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:40.760
I can't tell them I went 
home without getting them to fight me...

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:43.800
What do I do?!

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:48.850
<b>Beppu Akihiko
Born August 21st
Blood Type AB / Leo
Hobbies: Calligraphy, Flute
Likes: Rice balls</b>

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:02.640
First calligraphy of the year, and...

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:03.990
New Year's decorations?

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.740
The new year must be greeted with beauty.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:09.310
I'm writing our New Year's resolutions.

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:12.890
What do I do? What do I do?

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:13.680
I know.

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:16.590
I'll get them before they realize...

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:20.860
"I never know how to write 
the 'Yu' in 'Yufuin.'"

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:21.620
Here!

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:23.380
He's so fast!

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.380
He got another one!

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:26.010
En-chan, you still only have three?

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:27.800
So what if I do?

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.260
I've got three, too!

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:32.270
I haven't gotten a single card yet.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.810
I'm a shoo-in for the punishment.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:35.560
As am I.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.020
It's the short arms that do it.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.980
So the third member

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:45.450
of the designated shopper team will 
either be Yufuin-senpai or Yumoto.

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:51.540
Hakone's—

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:56.020
Me! Me me me!

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:56.910
—feels good.

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:59.210
I did it!

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:03.260
So the punishment falls 
to En, Ryuu, and Wom-san.

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:06.180
Hey, bad news!

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:09.190
Mr. Tawarayama's frozen over!

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:11.760
Hey.

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:12.590
Yeah?

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:15.900
What's the deal with dominos?

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:17.180
They make no sense.

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.820
In the end, you just knock them all over.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.730
I don't get the motivation behind it.

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:23.940
The enjoyment comes

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:28.700
from the thrill of accomplishment at 
seeing something through together—

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:28.700
Yeah, there's none.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:33.150
Speaking of, I don't get the motivation for 
being on those male cheer squads, either.

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:34.650
They're supposed to be encouraging people!

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:39.210
Yeah, guys in big jackets clapping on a 
3-3-7 beat doesn't really do it for me.

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:41.890
It's a tradition overflowing 
with manly spirit,

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:43.520
the bonds of male friendship,

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:45.670
and other such wonderful...

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:49.480
If they won't fight me, I'll 
bring the fight to them!

00:13:57.960 --> 00:14:00.520
Speaking of things I don't understand, 
what's with the way girls go shopping?

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.950
One, and... two!

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.640
I win!

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:11.240
I'm so sick of this.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.230
We've done karuta, fukuwarai, 
and top-spinning.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:16.010
This is the game we're stuck with.

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:18.980
Skipping makes no sense to me, either.

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:20.910
Yeah, I hear you!

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:24.130
You just bounce up and down, 
barely moving forward at all!

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:26.570
It also makes you more 
likely to trip and fall.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:29.350
I think it's a full-body expression of that

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:33.100
whoop-de-doo, pitter-patter, 
zing-zing feeling in your heart!

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:36.040
Whoop-de-doo, pitter-patter, zing-zing...

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.400
I haven't had a lot of that lately.

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:39.340
Same.

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:42.430
It's all been hurgh and brrr for me lately.

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:45.130
If you want whoop-de-doo, 
pitter-patter, zing-zing that bad,

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:46.690
I'll give it to you!

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:52.160
Snow, snow, snow, blizzard!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:54.620
Senpai!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.300
Skipping is great, huh?

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:58.800
Even though it's a blizzard, 
I'm having tons of fun!

00:14:58.800 --> 00:14:59.760
Yeah!

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:02.110
Why did I reject it for so long?

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.790
It's a crime that only kids do it!

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:07.380
I feel utterly whoop-de-doo, 
pitter-patter, zing-zing!

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.270
The attack's not working at all!

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:13.610
In that case, time for the "Slip and Fall in the Snow

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:16.600
That Encompasses College Entrance 
Exam-Takers Nationwide" Attack!

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:20.840
It's slippery here.

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:21.810
Be careful.

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:48.810
I haven't had a pitter-patter zing-zing 
feeling like this in a while.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:49.710
Yeah,

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.360
I guess we used to do stuff 
like that every day, huh?

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:55.040
Senpai!

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:56.010
Let's go!

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:03.700
I'm starting to forget which 
side got the punishment.

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:04.990
You know?

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:05.900
Yes.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:09.150
I did it!

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:10.820
Yeah, you did!

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:15.040
Then let me show you what 
happens when I get serious!

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:21.000
Hey, you're all playing!

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:26.040
Hey now, big brother's going 
to get serious now, too!

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:29.300
<b>Get within five meters
 of Gora-san.</b>

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:29.300
<b>Make eye contact with
 Gora-san five times.</b>

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.430
This is a true ward against evil.

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:39.300
<i>Why, you!</i>

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:41.360
That voice!

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:51.570
That sweater!

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:55.140
That's the Gora-san sweater 
we stayed up all night

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.060
knitting for Gora-san!

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:59.290
Unforgivable!

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:02.100
What is that Snowman Monster doing?

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:04.100
What's all the fuss?

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:07.500
Dadacha, call Snowman 
Monster back here at once!

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:08.970
G-Got it!

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:13.760
Why is it totally clear here?

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:17.190
It looks like the snow clouds are completely 
focused on the Kurotama Bath area.

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:20.720
Just a day into the new year and 
things are already getting strange...

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:23.760
I couldn't beat them.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:26.290
I suppose it's time for an artful suicide...

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.530
What are you doing here?!

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:30.440
Get back there and fight them!

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:32.170
That was surprising.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.900
Io, you know a lot about building igloos.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:37.660
I'm surprised you knew how 
to stack up the blocks!

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:41.950
To be honest, when I was a child,

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.620
I was known as "Igloo Maker Naru."

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.080
We're back!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.960
Hey, an igloo!

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:51.110
Igloo Maker Naru gave it his all!

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:53.340
Okay, everyone get inside!

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.370
Huh?

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:03.630
My leg!

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:05.400
It hurts, darn it!

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:07.860
What now?

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:10.520
We told you, we're not working today.

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:13.980
If you won't fight...

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:17.160
Then I'll destroy the igloo you built

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:19.450
and make it into a snowman!

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:21.580
You can't!

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:24.160
Igloo Maker Naru worked hard on that!

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:26.160
Then fight me!

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:27.820
You have no choice!

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:30.960
It's the first Love Making of the new year!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.580
Love Making!

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:39.180
The Sparkling Prince!

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.470
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.100
The Flashing Prince!

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:46.300
Battle Lover Cerulean!

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:48.900
The Piercing Prince!

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.180
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:54.250
The Roaring Prince!

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:56.520
Battle Lover Sulfur!

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:58.820
The Thrilling Prince!

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:00.930
Battle Lover Vesta!

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:05.410
This love-filled planet will 
not abide those who lack love!

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:09.120
Those who wield loveless 
power must kneel before love!

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:10.780
Love is power!

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:12.330
Love is hope!

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:14.050
Be born for love!

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:15.800
Give your life for love!

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:16.960
Love!

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:20.040
We are, forever, the heirs 
to the throne of love...

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:21.220
Battle Lovers!

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.070
Feel the power...

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:25.140
Of love!

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:29.180
You could never understand...

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:32.230
How it feels to keep rolling like a snowball,

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:34.770
then to melt without ever seeing spring.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.020
The same thing, year after year...

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:42.500
The feelings of a snowman

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:43.780
who can never escape winter...

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:50.380
But everyone loves snowmen.

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:53.250
They make our hearts feel 
like warm and toasty spring.

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:55.210
Warm and toasty spring?

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.200
As long as you live in everyone's hearts,

00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:01.420
even a snowman can see spring.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.780
I can see spring, too?

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:09.770
True Love Fountain!

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:21.900
Love is over!

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:31.040
Hey, it really was sunny 
out, just like spring!

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:34.310
When it's New Year, spring's not far away!

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:36.950
Getting to spend both New Year's Eve 
and New Year's Day with you guys

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:39.550
and my brother is a great 
sign of things to come!

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.510
I'm so grateful to that monster!

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:43.200
What?!

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:45.680
Even looking on the bright 
side has its limits!

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.540
Being grateful for a monster?!

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:50.020
What have we been doing wrong?

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:50.720
No...

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.420
the real question is, what 
is wrong with Hakone Yumoto?

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.660
If even this doesn't get the point through...

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:04.320
<b>Lucky
Sweet Sake
Free</b>

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:02.920
It's hot!

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:04.320
But delicious!

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.350
I don't know how you can drink that.

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:08.760
You can still taste the rice 
grains. I can't stand it.

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:09.640
Same here!

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:11.280
Senpai, we're pretty in sync this year!

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:12.780
No, we're not.

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:18.240
So, En-chan, what did you wish for?

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:21.660
For the kind of year where I 
can spend every day skipping.

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:22.210
Huh?

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:28.890
That's the guy...

00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:31.760
I hope he finds his spring this year.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.320
Brothers-senpai!

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:45.510
Happy New Year!

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:47.500
How dense can you get?

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:49.160
How have you not realized it?

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:50.620
Realized what?

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:52.200
Don't play dumb!

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:55.580
We're the ones who have been 
sending monsters after you!

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.490
Don't you get it yet?

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:00.750
We, the brothers, are...

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:11.550
The twin stars shining in the heavens!

00:22:11.550 --> 00:22:12.600
Salty Sol!

00:22:13.170 --> 00:22:14.520
Melty Luna!

00:22:16.090 --> 00:22:18.850
Galaxy Idols: The VEPPer!

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:58.770
Next Time

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:58.770
The Chemical Substance of Love

00:23:54.920 --> 00:23:57.100
Next time: "The Chemical Substance
 of Love!"

00:23:57.100 --> 00:23:58.500
Love Making!
